# connectivity statistic (xk4.cpp, instrumented copy of xk_par.c)
$ ./xk4 6 ... -> NO_6_EXCHANGE nodes=9540881 seconds=71.4
NODESTAT nodes=9540881 connected=97026        # 1.02% of visited partial sets have a
                                              # connected (A, T(A)) bipartite graph
# Any *minimal* improving exchange must be connected (a disconnected one splits into
# two exchanges, one of them improving with smaller k; k<=8 is already excluded).
# So a correct connected-set enumeration could cut the k=9 tree by ~2 orders of
# magnitude.  Two ESU-style prototypes were written and both FAILED the brute-force
# self-test on random small instances (e.g. 34 vs 19, 46 vs 37), so nothing of that
# kind is archived or used for any claim.
